      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Suppose S.P. ₹120 gives x% profit and ₹80 gives x% loss. Then C.P. must satisfy 120/C −1 = 1−80/C.\n120−C = C−80 → C=100.\nIn this special symmetric case, midpoint appears because the profit/loss percentages share the same C.P.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
